{"id":"PO-1","kind":"missing","severity":"blocking","requirement":"none","title":"No requirement gives the user a view of one order and its lines","why":"Brief: 'add, edit, and remove order lines' and 'order lines belonging to each order'. R-09 stops at a list ('shows number, customer name, date and total') and R-03 shows only 'the customer's orders with their totals'. R-11, R-12 and R-13 act on lines, but nothing says where the lines are shown, how an order is opened, or that a line total or the notes are ever displayed. R-14 computes a line total that no criterion shows. Walking the flow customer &gt; create order &gt; add lines &gt; see total, the step after R-06 has no requirement, so the tester has nothing to test it against. R-07 notes can be edited but never read.","suggested":"### R-28 [MUST] View an order\n- Creating an order opens it; the order list and the customer detail each open an order when the user selects it.\n- The order view shows the number, customer name, date, notes, every line with description, quantity, unit price and line total in the order they were added (A-08), and the order total.\n- From the order view the user can edit the order (R-07), add, edit and remove lines (R-11 to R-13) and delete the order (R-08).\n- The user can reach the customer list and the order list from every screen.","proven":true},
{"id":"PO-2","kind":"missing","severity":"blocking","requirement":"R-20","title":"Unreadable stored data leaves the user in a state with no way out","why":"R-20: 'the app shows an error and does not write over it'. No criterion says what the user can do next. Export is LATER (R-25), so the data cannot be taken out, and starting again would need the browser's developer tools. Every main flow stays closed for good, or, if the lists render empty, the first save writes over the data R-20 protects. Brief: 'useful empty or error states'. This is a dead end under checklist item 2.","suggested":"### R-20 [MUST] Unreadable stored data is not overwritten\n- If the saved data cannot be read, or was saved by a newer version of the app, the app shows an error instead of the lists; nothing can be added or changed, so nothing is written over the data.\n- The error says what happened and offers two ways out: copy the stored text, or start with empty data.\n- Starting with empty data needs a confirmation that says the old data will be lost; only then is the stored data replaced.","proven":true},
{"id":"PO-3","kind":"missing","severity":"advisory","requirement":"R-17","title":"No way to leave a form without saving","why":"R-17: 'nothing is saved until all fields are valid'. No requirement offers Cancel, so a user who opened a form by mistake, or cannot satisfy a rule, has no stated way out. R-02 says of an invalid edit that 'the old values stay', but R-07 and R-12 say nothing of the kind.","suggested":"Add to R-17:\n- Every form has a Cancel action that closes it and discards what was typed; the saved values stay as they were.\n- An invalid edit of an order or a line is not saved and the old values stay, as in R-02.","proven":true},
{"id":"PO-4","kind":"unclear","severity":"advisory","requirement":"R-04","title":"Delete customer: confirm first or refuse first, and no pointer to the way out","why":"R-04 has 'The user must confirm before a customer is deleted' and 'A customer who has orders cannot be deleted; the app says why and how many orders block it'. It reads two ways: confirm and then be refused, or be refused at once. The message also does not say how to proceed, though R-18 holds empty states to saying 'what to do next'. The rule itself was decided (Q-01) and is not reopened here.","suggested":"Replace the R-04 criteria with:\n- If the customer has no orders, the user must confirm before the customer is deleted.\n- If the customer has orders, the app asks for no confirmation; it says the customer cannot be deleted, how many orders block it, and that those orders must be deleted first. No data changes.","proven":true},
{"id":"PO-5","kind":"risk","severity":"advisory","requirement":"R-25","title":"With export LATER, the only copy of the data is one browser profile","why":"Implied line: 'data must survive a reload and must never be lost silently'. A-01: 'Data stays on the device'. A-09: 'Deleting is permanent'. R-25 is LATER, so clearing site data or changing browser removes everything with no warning and no backup. It does not block first use, so LATER can stand, but the user should be told. What settles it: the human either keeps R-25 LATER with the assumption below or moves R-25 to MUST.","suggested":"- **A-11** The data lives only in this browser on this device. Clearing the browser's site data removes it and there is no backup until R-25 exists. The customer list shows a one-line note saying so.","proven":false},
{"id":"PO-6","kind":"priority","severity":"advisory","requirement":"R-10","title":"R-10 asks for both filter and search where the brief says one or the other","why":"Brief: 'Keep the scope light' and 'search or filter customers and orders'. R-10 requires both: 'filtered by one customer and searched by order number or customer name'. Customer orders are already visible in the customer detail (R-03), so the filter is not needed for first use. What settles it: the human says whether both mechanisms are wanted in the first version.","suggested":"### R-10 [MUST] Search orders\n- Typing in the search box shows only orders whose number or customer name contains the text, case-insensitive, ignoring leading and trailing spaces.\n- An empty search shows all orders.\n\n### R-29 [LATER] Filter orders by one customer","proven":false},
{"id":"PO-7","kind":"unclear","severity":"advisory","requirement":"R-14","title":"R-14 is worded around how the amount is computed","why":"R-14: 'computed in whole cents with no rounding error'. Whole cents is an implementation choice already in A-04. The user can only observe the amount, so the example is the real criterion.","suggested":"- A line total is quantity × unit price and is exact to the cent (for example 3 × 0.10 shows 0.30, and 3 × 19.99 shows 59.97).","proven":true},
{"id":"PO-8","kind":"unclear","severity":"advisory","requirement":"R-16","title":"R-16 names an API instead of what the user sees","why":"R-16: 'formatted with `Intl.NumberFormat`'. A user cannot observe that, while they can observe the separators and the euro sign. A-04 already says the format follows the browser's locale.","suggested":"- Every amount is shown with two decimals and the euro sign, with separators that follow the browser's language (for example 1,234.50 in English and 1.234,50 in Romanian).","proven":true},
{"id":"PO-9","kind":"unclear","severity":"advisory","requirement":"R-19","title":"Second criterion of R-19 is a storage design, not something a user sees","why":"R-19: 'All data is stored under one `localStorage` key as JSON with a schema version'. No user can observe this, and the data model sketch already states it. The first criterion alone is the user-visible requirement.","suggested":"Delete the second criterion of R-19; the one-key format stays in the Data model sketch.","proven":true},
{"id":"PO-10","kind":"unclear","severity":"advisory","requirement":"R-22","title":"R-22 leaves phone, address and the search text out of its list","why":"R-22 names 'Any name, email, description or note'. A-02 makes phone and address 'free text' too, and search text may be echoed back in a no-results message (R-18). ADR-002 states the rule without exceptions: 'user text is never rendered as HTML'. A tester working from the list would miss two fields.","suggested":"- Any text the user typed, in any field or search box, containing HTML such as `&lt;b&gt;x&lt;/b&gt;` is displayed literally, never interpreted.","proven":true},
{"id":"PO-11","kind":"missing","severity":"advisory","requirement":"R-18","title":"Empty states miss the customer with no orders and order creation with no customers","why":"R-18 lists 'No customers, no orders, an order with no lines and a search with no results'. Three states fall outside it. A customer detail with no orders (R-03) is one. Creating an order when no customer exists is another: R-06 says only 'An order can only be created for an existing customer', and on an empty order list the next step is to add a customer, not an order. The third is a customer filter with no match (R-10), which is not a search. Brief: 'useful empty or error states'.","suggested":"Add to R-18:\n- A customer with no orders shows a message offering to create the first order for that customer.\n- With no customers yet, the order list says a customer must be added first and links to the customer form; an order cannot be started.\n- A filter or search on orders with no match says so and offers to clear it.","proven":true},
{"id":"PO-12","kind":"missing","severity":"advisory","requirement":"R-06","title":"No rule for the order date or the notes","why":"R-06: 'the date of today, which the user can change'. R-07 lets the user change date and notes. R-17 needs a message 'naming the rule it broke', but neither field has a rule: a cleared date, an impossible date or very long notes are all undefined, and R-09 sorts by that date. R-06 also does not say whether notes can be entered at creation, though the data model has them. Brief: 'basic validation'.","suggested":"Add to R-06:\n- The date is required and must be a real calendar date; past and future dates are allowed.\n- The form also accepts optional notes, up to 500 characters after trimming; the same rules apply in R-07.","proven":true},
{"id":"PO-13","kind":"unclear","severity":"advisory","requirement":"R-11","title":"What the user may type as a price is not defined","why":"R-11: 'a unit price from 0.00 to 1 000 000.00 with at most two decimals'. A-04: 'display formatting uses the browser's locale'. A user on a comma locale sees 12,50 € and may type 12,50, or type 1,000.50 in English. The requirement reads two ways: rejected, or accepted as a different amount. A wrongly read amount would change totals with no warning. R-12 also does not say how the current price appears in the edit field.","suggested":"Add to R-11:\n- The unit price accepts a dot or a comma as the decimal separator and no thousands separators; anything else shows an error next to the field.\n- When a line is edited, the unit price field shows the saved price with two decimals.","proven":true},
{"id":"PO-14","kind":"risk","severity":"advisory","requirement":"R-13","title":"Removing a line has no confirmation while deleting anything else does","why":"R-04 and R-08 require confirmation. R-13 says only 'Removing a line takes it out of the order', and A-09 says 'Deleting is permanent; there is no undo or trash'. One misclick loses a line for good. It may be a deliberate choice for speed, but nothing says so. What settles it: the human chooses to confirm, or records that no confirmation is intended.","suggested":"### R-13 [MUST] Remove an order line\n- After confirmation the line is taken out of the order and the order total updates at once.","proven":false},
{"id":"PO-15","kind":"unclear","severity":"advisory","requirement":"R-21","title":"After a failed save, what happens to what the user typed is not stated","why":"R-21: 'the app shows an error and the change is not shown as saved'. This can be met by closing the form and dropping the input, while AGENTS.md rule 6 says 'never lose user data silently'. With a full quota the user also has no stated next step.","suggested":"Add to R-21:\n- The form stays open with what the user typed, so the save can be retried; the error says the browser's storage is full or unavailable and that deleting data frees space.","proven":true},
{"id":"PO-16","kind":"risk","severity":"advisory","requirement":"none","title":"Two tabs of the app may lose changes or repeat an order number","why":"A-01 says 'One user, one browser' but says nothing about two tabs, which one user can easily open. If each tab holds its own copy, the later save overwrites the earlier one. Implied line: 'must never be lost silently'. R-06: 'Order numbers are unique and never reused'. What settles it: the human says whether two tabs are in scope; the outcome also depends on the design, which does not exist yet.","suggested":"Add to R-19:\n- With the app open in two tabs, a change saved in one tab is not lost when the other tab saves, and order numbers stay unique.\nOr, if out of scope, extend A-01: Only one tab is open at a time; two tabs are not supported.","proven":false},
{"id":"PO-17","kind":"risk","severity":"advisory","requirement":"none","title":"Nothing says whether two customers can have the same name","why":"R-01 sets only a length for the name. Two customers called the same would look identical in the R-10 customer filter and could be confused when creating an order (R-06), which A-06 makes costly because 'An order's customer cannot be changed'. What settles it: the human says whether duplicates are allowed.","suggested":"- **A-12** Two customers may have the same name or email; wherever a customer is picked, the email is shown next to the name.","proven":false},
{"id":"PO-18","kind":"unclear","severity":"advisory","requirement":"R-01","title":"R-01 omits phone and address, and the 200-character limit is in no criterion","why":"R-01: 'saves a name (1 to 100 characters after trimming) and an optional email'. A-02 lists 'email, phone, address (all optional, free text up to 200 characters)', and R-02 edits phone and address 'The same rules as R-01'. R-01 has no rule for them, so the create form may lack two fields the edit form has, and a 300-character address has no defined result.","suggested":"Replace the first criterion of R-01 with:\n- Given the customer form, when the user saves a name (1 to 100 characters after trimming) and optionally an email, phone and address (each up to 200 characters), then the customer appears in the list.","proven":true},
{"id":"PO-19","kind":"unclear","severity":"advisory","requirement":"R-10","title":"R-10 lacks the search details R-05 spells out","why":"R-05 says 'ignoring leading and trailing spaces' and 'An empty search shows all customers'. R-10 says only 'case-insensitive; both apply together'. The two searches may behave differently, and neither an empty search nor clearing the filter is defined. If PO-6 is accepted, its text covers this and only the search part applies.","suggested":"Add to R-10:\n- Search ignores leading and trailing spaces; an empty search and no chosen customer show all orders.","proven":true}
